<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21186] Client Can Bypass Permission Checks During File Layout Swap</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21186</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Swapping the layouts (data placement) of two files should only be allowed after verifying that the user has permission to access both files.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The MDS already prevents clients from setting the internal flag SWAP_LAYOUTS_MDS_RELEASE, as it is reserved for server-side HSM release operations and bypasses normal permission checks.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However, a similar internal flag, SWAP_LAYOUTS_MDS_HSM, was not properly restricted. A modified client could set this flag directly and bypass the normal permission checks when swapping file layouts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As a result, a user could swap layouts of files they are not authorized to modify, including immutable files or files owned by other users.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Expected Behavior: The MDS should prevent clients from setting internal-only flags and ensure that normal permission checks are always enforced for client-initiated layout swaps.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
